    [BugFix]: handle MemCache allocation sentinel values (#18501)
    
    Treat zero as an SSD hit and filter UINT64_MAX allocation failures
    before signed GVA conversion and copy. Cover full blocks, partial
    blocks, and DSpark prefix saves.
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Adapt MemCache layerwise saves to its allocation return values:
    
    - `0`: allocation failure.
    - `UINT64_MAX`: readable SSD-only hit; skip writing.
    - Normal GVA: proceed with writing.
    
    Filter both sentinel values before conversion to `np.int64`, copying,
    and write-finish notification. This prevents integer overflow and
    invalid writes when an existing key has only an SSD replica.
    
    The change covers full blocks, partial blocks, and DSpark prefix saves,
    with corresponding UT coverage.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce any user-facing change?
    
    Yes. MemCache SSD hits are skipped without being treated as allocation
    failures. Existing allocation failure handling is preserved.
    
    No API signatures or configuration options are changed. This requires
    the corresponding MemCache allocation sentinel support.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Ran `test_pool_worker.py` and `test_dspark_prefix_cache.py` in the
    `memcache-yy-service` container using CPU mocks: **154 passed, 0 failed,
    0 skipped**.
    - All six sentinel-related regression cases passed, covering full
    blocks, partial blocks, SSD-only hits, and mixed SSD/memory allocation
    results.
    
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/8cc9aa5ad350f6f80cf3bebb298d410803ff75a9
    
    Signed-off-by: yyang728 <2533623867@qq.com>

